  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Combating Arthropod Pest for Better Health, Food and Climate Resilience</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The programme, Combating Arthropod Pest for Better Health, Food and Resilience to Climate Change (CAP-Africa) will conduct research which aims to improve the health, food security and climate resilience of people of East Africa.  CAP-AFRICA will implement activities in Kenya, Ethiopia, Uganda and Tanzania.  Programme period: 2018-2023. It(the project) provides support to MSc and PhD to conduct research related to health  and management of marine resources.</narrative>
  </description>
